# Line endings
# ------------
# The repository already stores every text file with LF — `git ls-files --eol`
# reports i/lf for all 238 of them — but core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks
# them out as CRLF. Prettier's endOfLine default is "lf", so `npm run
# format:check` flags essentially every file on a Windows clone while the same
# command passes in CI on Linux. Pinning eol=lf makes the working tree match the
# index on every platform, so the local and CI results agree.
#
# This does not rewrite history or produce a normalisation diff: the index is
# already LF, so only the working tree changes on the next checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.mp4 binary

# mirror/ is a byte-for-byte capture of the live caaciorg.com and must never be
# rewritten — the whole point of that tree is that the served bytes match the
# original site. mirror/zh/events/index.html genuinely contains mixed line
# endings, and normalising it would change bytes the mirror exists to preserve.
#
# Last matching pattern wins in gitattributes, so this block stays at the bottom
# to override the `* text=auto eol=lf` rule above for everything under mirror/.
mirror/** -text
